coco-pipe requires braindecode 2.0. Frozen embeddings do not change: with the released LaBraM, CBraMod, LUNA and BIOT weights they match those of braindecode 1.8.1 within float rounding. Frozen LaBraM reads its pretrained final norm (`use_mean_pooling=False`), since braindecode 2.0's default passes the tokens through a readout norm that only fine-tuning trains, and LUNA still refuses a window that does not divide into its 40-sample patches, which braindecode 2.0 would pad.
